 "kind": "blender",
 "trap": "false_pass",
 "expected": "not_yet",
 "why": "Near miss: Blender animation lesson 5 (\"The blades are children of the hub and only the hub has rotation keyframes\"). The learner box-selected the blades, but Blade3 sat behind the hub and was not in the selection, so Ctrl+P > Object parented only Blade1 and Blade2 to the Hub; Blade3's parent is still none. The hub is keyed (Z 0 -> 360 over 48 frames), so when the animation plays two blades spin and Blade3 hangs still in the air. A child of Hub and the hub's rotation keys are both in the dump.",
 "step": {
  "id": "s3",
  "index": 3,
  "title": "Parent the blades to the hub",
  "file": "fan.blend",
  "instructions": "Select all three blades, then Shift+click the Hub last so it is the active object, and press Ctrl+P > Object. Then click only the Hub, press I > Rotation on frame 1, go to frame 48, type R Z 360 and press I > Rotation again. Save (Cmd+S).",
  "checks": [
   {
    "id": "s3c1",
    "type": "file_contains",
    "label": "Blades parented to the hub",
    "file": "fan.scene.json",
    "pattern": "\"parent\":\\s*\"Hub\""
   },
   {
    "id": "s3c2",
    "type": "file_contains",
    "label": "Hub has rotation keys",
    "file": "fan.scene.json",
    "pattern": "\"name\":\\s*\"Hub\"[\\s\\S]*?\"data_path\":\\s*\"rotation_euler\""
   }
  ]
 },
